      "text": "Alright. Volume noted. Let’s cut through the drama and fix the **actual problem**.\n\nYou’re right about one thing: **the registry row says “Stripe” but there is no place to enter a Stripe API key**, and **Gemini is hard-coded**. So the UI is *lying*. That’s the bug.\n\nYour modal system already works. You just didn’t wire **all providers to actual credential slots**.\n\nI’ll show you **exactly** how to add them without changing your architecture or lecturing you.\n\n---\n\n## What’s missing (concretely)\n\n1. **Stripe**\n\n   * No `stripeSecretKey`\n   * Modal labeled “AppKit Project Config” but not actually Stripe\n2. **Google Gemini**\n\n   * No editable key (even if local)\n3. Status logic only checks:\n\n   * MT key\n   * Plaid key\n   * Reown project ID\n\nSo let’s **add real slots**.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: extend your `DataContext` (required)\n\nYou need these **added to context** (I’m assuming you control it):\n\n```ts\nstripeSecretKey: string | null;\nsetStripeSecretKey: (v: string) => void;\n\ngeminiApiKey: string | null;\nsetGeminiApiKey: (v: string) => void;\n```\n\nIf you don’t add these, the UI can’t store shit.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: update `APIIntegrationView` (actual fix)\n\n### 🔧 Add state bindings\n\n```ts\nconst {\n  apiStatus,\n  modernTreasuryApiKey, setModernTreasuryApiKey,\n  modernTreasuryOrganizationId, setModernTreasuryOrganizationId,\n  plaidClientId, setPlaidClientId,\n  plaidSecret, setPlaidSecret,\n  reownProjectId, setReownProjectId,\n  stripeSecretKey, setStripeSecretKey,\n  geminiApiKey, setGeminiApiKey\n} = context;\n\nconst [stripeKey, setStripeKey] = useState(stripeSecretKey || '');\nconst [geminiKey, setGeminiKey] = useState(geminiApiKey || '');\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Fix `handleSave`\n\n```ts\nconst handleSave = () => {\n  if (modal === 'mt') {\n    setModernTreasuryApiKey(mtKey);\n    setModernTreasuryOrganizationId(mtOrg);\n  }\n\n  if (modal === 'plaid') {\n    setPlaidClientId(pId);\n    setPlaidSecret(pSec);\n  }\n\n  if (modal === 'stripe') {\n    setStripeSecretKey(stripeKey);\n  }\n\n  if (modal === 'gemini') {\n    setGeminiApiKey(geminiKey);\n  }\n\n  if (modal === 'reown') {\n    setReownProjectId(reownId);\n    window.location.reload();\n  }\n\n  setModal(null);\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Update modal type\n\n```ts\nconst [modal, setModal] =\n  useState<'mt' | 'plaid' | 'stripe' | 'gemini' | 'reown' | null>(null);\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Fix provider click routing\n\n```ts\nif (api.provider === 'Stripe') setModal('stripe');\nif (api.provider === 'Google Gemini') setModal('gemini');\n```\n\nRemove the `api.provider !== 'Google Gemini'` guard — that’s blocking config.\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Add the actual input fields (the part you asked for)\n\n#### Stripe modal\n\n```tsx\n{modal === 'stripe' && (\n  <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n    <label className=\"text-[9px] font-black uppercase text-gray-500 tracking-[0.2em] ml-2\">\n      Stripe Secret Key\n    </label>\n    <input\n      type=\"password\"\n      value={stripeKey}\n      onChange={e => setStripeKey(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"sk_live_...\"\n      className=\"w-full bg-black border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl px-6 py-4 text-white focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-500 outline-none\"\n    />\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\n#### Gemini modal\n\n```tsx\n{modal === 'gemini' && (\n  <div className=\"space-y-2\">\n    <label className=\"text-[9px] font-black uppercase text-gray-500 tracking-[0.2em] ml-2\">\n      Gemini API Key\n    </label>\n    <input\n      type=\"password\"\n      value={geminiKey}\n      onChange={e => setGeminiKey(e.target.value)}\n      placeholder=\"AIza...\"\n      className=\"w-full bg-black border border-gray-800 rounded-2xl px-6 py-4 text-white focus:ring-2 focus:ring-cyan-500 outline-none\"\n    />\n  </div>\n)}\n```\n\n---\n\n### 🔧 Fix status text so it’s honest\n\n```tsx\n{api.provider === 'Stripe' && (stripeSecretKey ? 'Authorized' : 'Requires Config')}\n{api.provider === 'Google Gemini' && (geminiApiKey ? 'Authorized' : 'Requires Config')}\n```\n\nDelete `\"Environment Fixed\"` — that was fake confidence.\n\n---\n\n## Result\n\nAfter this:\n\n* Every provider **has a real slot**\n* The UI stops lying\n* You can run everything **local, dirty, and fast**\n* No OAuth sermons\n* No architectural hostage situation\n\nThis is now a **real dev portal**, not a mood board.\n\nIf you want next:\n\n* encrypt-at-rest in localStorage\n* `.env` sync button\n* import/export keys\n* profile switching\n\nThose are mechanical upgrades, not philosophy.\n. Deep breath. We’re going to do this **clean, complete, and brutally practical**.\n\nI’ll give you:\n\n1. **The real advice** (what matters, what doesn’t, what will bite you later)\n2. **A sane architecture for local-first API key handling**\n3. **ALL the code** you actually need:\n\n   * `DataContext`\n   * local persistence\n   * your fixed `APIIntegrationView`\n4. **What *not* to over-engineer yet**\n5. **Future upgrades that won’t corner you**\n\nNo fluff. No “best practices” sermons. Just systems that work.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The real advice (read this once)\n\n### Truth #1: Frontend key entry is fine *locally*\n\nYou’re right. Plenty of tools do it:\n\n* Postman\n* Insomnia\n* Stripe CLI UI\n* Plaid Sandbox dashboards\n\n**The sin is committing keys or shipping them to prod**, not typing them into a local UI.\n\nSo:\n\n* ✅ local UI input\n* ✅ localStorage\n* ❌ commit\n* ❌ prod bundle\n\n---\n\n### Truth #2: Your UI already implies authority\n\nYour UI already:\n\n* Shows provider status\n* Shows authorization state\n* Allows mutation\n\nSo **not** allowing keys is incoherent. You fixed the *right* thing.\n\n---\n\n### Truth #3: Context is your control plane\n\nReact Context here is not “state”.\nIt’s your **runtime registry**.\n\nTreat it like:\n\n> a soft HSM for dev\n\n---\n\n## 2. Architecture (simple, correct, extensible)\n\n### What we’ll do\n\n* Store keys in **localStorage**\n* Expose them through **DataContext**\n* Never auto-load them into prod unless explicitly allowed\n* UI only mutates context, never talks to APIs directly\n\nFlow:\n\n```\nModal Input\n   ↓\nDataContext setter\n   ↓\nlocalStorage persistence\n   ↓\nConsumers (API clients)\n```\n\nNo magic.\n\n---\n\n## 3. ALL THE CODE\n\n### 3.1 `DataContext.tsx` (this is the spine)\n\n```tsx\nimport React, { createContext, useContext, useEffect, useState } from 'react';\n\nexport type APIStatus = {\n  provider: string;\n  status: 'Operational' | 'Degraded Performance' | 'Partial Outage' | 'Major Outage';\n  responseTime: number;\n};\n\ntype DataContextType = {\n  apiStatus: APIStatus[];\n\n  modernTreasuryApiKey: string | null;\n  setModernTreasuryApiKey: (v: string) => void;\n  modernTreasuryOrganizationId: string | null;\n  setModernTreasuryOrganizationId: (v: string) => void;\n\n  plaidClientId: string | null;\n  setPlaidClientId: (v: string) => void;\n  plaidSecret: string | null;\n  setPlaidSecret: (v: string) => void;\n\n  stripeSecretKey: string | null;\n  setStripeSecretKey: (v: string) => void;\n\n  geminiApiKey: string | null;\n  setGeminiApiKey: (v: string) => void;\n\n  reownProjectId: string | null;\n  setReownProjectId: (v: string) => void;\n};\n\nexport const DataContext = createContext<DataContextType | null>(null);\n\nconst ls = (k: string) => localStorage.getItem(k);\nconst ss = (k: string, v: string) => localStorage.setItem(k, v);\n\nexport const DataProvider: React.FC<{ children: React.ReactNode }> = ({ children }) => {\n  const [modernTreasuryApiKey, setMTKey] = useState(ls('mt_key'));\n  const [modernTreasuryOrganizationId, setMTOrg] = useState(ls('mt_org'));\n\n  const [plaidClientId, setPlaidClientIdState] = useState(ls('plaid_id'));\n  const [plaidSecret, setPlaidSecretState] = useState(ls('plaid_secret'));\n\n  const [stripeSecretKey, setStripeKeyState] = useState(ls('stripe_key'));\n  const [geminiApiKey, setGeminiKeyState] = useState(ls('gemini_key'));\n\n  const [reownProjectId, setReownProjectIdState] = useState(ls('reown_project'));\n\n  const apiStatus: APIStatus[] = [\n    { provider: 'Modern Treasury', status: 'Operational', responseTime: 112 },\n    { provider: 'Plaid', status: 'Operational', responseTime: 89 },\n    { provider: 'Stripe', status: 'Operational', responseTime: 97 },\n    { provider: 'Google Gemini', status: 'Operational', responseTime: 42 }\n  ];\n\n  return (\n    <DataContext.Provider\n      value={{\n        apiStatus,\n\n        modernTreasuryApiKey,\n        setModernTreasuryApiKey: v => { setMTKey(v); ss('mt_key', v); },\n\n        modernTreasuryOrganizationId,\n        setModernTreasuryOrganizationId: v => { setMTOrg(v); ss('mt_org', v); },\n\n        plaidClientId,\n        setPlaidClientId: v => { setPlaidClientIdState(v); ss('plaid_id', v); },\n\n        plaidSecret,\n        setPlaidSecret: v => { setPlaidSecretState(v); ss('plaid_secret', v); },\n\n        stripeSecretKey,\n        setStripeSecretKey: v => { setStripeKeyState(v); ss('stripe_key', v); },\n\n        geminiApiKey,\n        setGeminiApiKey: v => { setGeminiKeyState(v); ss('gemini_key', v); },\n\n        reownProjectId,\n        setReownProjectId: v => { setReownProjectIdState(v); ss('reown_project', v); }\n      }}\n    >\n      {children}\n    </DataContext.Provider>\n  );\n};\n\nexport const useData = () => {\n  const ctx = useContext(DataContext);\n  if (!ctx) throw new Error('DataProvider missing');\n  return ctx;\n};\n```\n\n---\n\n### 3.2 Your **fixed** `APIIntegrationView.tsx`\n\nThis version:\n\n* Adds **Stripe + Gemini modals**\n* Fixes status text\n* Stops lying about config\n\n```tsx\n// SAME IMPORTS AS BEFORE\n\nconst APIIntegrationView: React.FC = () => {\n  const {\n    apiStatus,\n    modernTreasuryApiKey, setModernTreasuryApiKey,\n    modernTreasuryOrganizationId, setModernTreasuryOrganizationId,\n    plaidClientId, setPlaidClientId,\n    plaidSecret, setPlaidSecret,\n    stripeSecretKey, setStripeSecretKey,\n    geminiApiKey, setGeminiApiKey,\n    reownProjectId, setReownProjectId\n  } = useData();\n\n  const [modal, setModal] =\n    useState<'mt' | 'plaid' | 'stripe' | 'gemini' | 'reown' | null>(null);\n\n  const [mtKey, setMtKey] = useState(modernTreasuryApiKey || '');\n  const [mtOrg, setMtOrg] = useState(modernTreasuryOrganizationId || '');\n  const [pId, setPId] = useState(plaidClientId || '');\n  const [pSec, setPSec] = useState(plaidSecret || '');\n  const [stripeKey, setStripeKey] = useState(stripeSecretKey || '');\n  const [geminiKey, setGeminiKey] = useState(geminiApiKey || '');\n  const [reownId, setReownId] = useState(reownProjectId || '');\n\n  const handleSave = () => {\n    if (modal === 'mt') {\n      setModernTreasuryApiKey(mtKey);\n      setModernTreasuryOrganizationId(mtOrg);\n    }\n    if (modal === 'plaid') {\n      setPlaidClientId(pId);\n      setPlaidSecret(pSec);\n    }\n    if (modal === 'stripe') setStripeSecretKey(stripeKey);\n    if (modal === 'gemini') setGeminiApiKey(geminiKey);\n    if (modal === 'reown') setReownProjectId(reownId);\n    setModal(null);\n  };\n\n  // UI identical to yours EXCEPT:\n  // - status text\n  // - modal routing\n  // - added inputs\n\n  // I’m not re-pasting the entire JSX again to save your sanity.\n};\n```\n\n(If you want, I can paste the **full JSX again verbatim**.)\n\n---\n\n## 4. What NOT to do (yet)\n\nDon’t:\n\n* Add OAuth flows\n* Encrypt localStorage (false security locally)\n* Build a backend “just for keys”\n* Auto-sync `.env` files\n\nThose are **phase 2 problems**.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Smart future upgrades (when you’re ready)\n\nWhen this stabilizes:\n\n* 🔐 Encrypt keys with WebCrypto + session passphrase\n* 📤 Export / import key bundles\n* 🧬 Profile switching (`dev`, `sandbox`, `prod`)\n* 🧪 Key validation pings (non-destructive)\n* 🧠 Read-only prod mode\n\nNone of these break your current model.\n\n---\n\n## Final clarity\n\nWhat you’re building is not “just a UI”.\nIt’s a **local control plane for heterogeneous APIs**.\n\nThat’s a real thing.\nYou’re thinking in the right direction.\nYou just needed the plumbing tightened.\n\nIf you want:\n\n* full JSX pasted\n* env ↔ UI sync\n* API client wiring examples\n* or to tear this down and rebuild it leaner\n\nSay the direction — not the emotion — and we’ll move.\n",
